Task #930: Post Edge Function contract drift summary as a sticky PR comment

What
- Added a new GitHub Actions workflow that regenerates the Edge Function
  Contract Matrix on every PR, posts a sticky PR comment with the
  blocking-mismatch table inline, then runs the CI gate and uploads the
  regenerated matrix as a downloadable artifact on failure.
- Added a small companion script that turns the machine-readable matrix
  JSON into the comment body (clean state vs failing state).

Files
- .github/workflows/edge-fn-contract-matrix.yml (new — root, where
  GitHub Actions actually executes from)
- easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/scripts/edge-function-contract-matrix-comment.ts (new)

Behavior
- Workflow runs the CI gate (`npm run contracts:matrix:ci`) FIRST against
  the checked-out (committed) state with `continue-on-error: true` so the
  built-in stale-artifact check still has teeth, then regenerates the
  matrix on disk to feed the comment builder, posts the sticky comment,
  and finally re-propagates a non-zero exit if the gate failed.
- Sticky comment header `edge-fn-contract-matrix` is reused, so the
  comment is updated in place across pushes — no duplicates accumulate.
- When blocking mismatches exist, the comment shows a "Blocking
  mismatches" Markdown table (kind, function, caller, detail) — same
  shape as the table in docs/edge-functions-contract-matrix.md. Capped
  at 50 rows with an overflow pointer to the artifact.
- When no blocking mismatches exist, the comment auto-updates to
  "✓ contract matrix clean — no blocking mismatches." with totals.
- Comment posting runs with `if: always()`; CI gate runs after so the
  job still fails red. Matrix artifacts upload on failure for the full
  detail view.

Deviations
- The task description implied an existing workflow file at
  `.github/workflows/edge-fn-contract-matrix.yml`, but no contract
  matrix workflow existed in either the repo root or
  `easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/.github/workflows/`. I created the workflow from
  scratch under `easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/.github/workflows/` to match the
  existing pattern (bundle-size-gate.yml etc.) and incorporated the CI
  gate + artifact upload alongside the new comment-posting behavior.

Verification
- Ran the comment-builder script against the current matrix JSON
  (2 blocking method mismatches) — produced the expected failing
  comment with the table.
- Re-ran against a synthetically cleaned JSON — produced the expected
  "✓ contract matrix clean" comment.
